[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Charged Junction Recovery Qualification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONV-SPICE-JUNCTION-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Recover the charged junction without false physical success
STATEMENT: >>>
The admitted SPICE diode profile shall support bounded source and Gmin continuation through the existing CPU providers. Qualification shall first demonstrate a failed direct solve under the same Newton iteration budget, then compare recovered bias against an independent inverse-Shockley and KCL oracle. Successful Gmin recovery shall remove the artificial shunt. Physically impossible reverse-current bias shall remain a failure under both recovery strategies.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: tests/spice_diode_continuation.rs exercises LU, QR and faer with real depletion/diffusion parameters, eight direct iterations, rejected source stages, final unit source scale and final unregularized Gmin recovery. The two finite scenarios do not establish universal convergence, BJT/MOS recovery, nonlinear energy accuracy or all requested-transient policies. Coverage is inherited only for separately measured numerical scopes; these tests do not provide new whole-core branch coverage.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONV-BJT-COMPOSITE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Qualify composite BJT recovery and physical refusal
STATEMENT: >>>
Qualification of the admitted diode-connected NPN/PNP composition shall demonstrate an actual bounded direct-Newton failure, explicit exhaustion of a coarse source-step policy, successful finer source stepping and Gmin recovery against independent inverse-Ebers-Moll voltage and KCL oracles, and refusal of impossible reverse injection. Artificial shunt removal shall be challenged by physical tolerances tighter than its unrecovered contribution.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: BjtContinuationNativeTests uses both LU/faer through the generated frontend and public client. Eight iterations are held fixed. Source minimum scale 1e-6 is intentionally insufficient; the qualified finer policy permits 1e-12 within 128 stages. Gmin uses 1 S to 1e-9 S warm starts, then the mandatory unregularized solve. Nonzero junction/transit storage is retained in the composite. Public API results do not expose internal stage counters, so no counter-coverage claim follows. This is finite composite recovery evidence, not arbitrary transistor circuits or universal convergence.
<<<
